] [17592186077468 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186077469 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186077468 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186077470 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186077468 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186077471 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186077468 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186077472 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186077468 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186077473 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186077468 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186077468 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186077468 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186077472 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186077468 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "cd9bfa65-ff88-5011-a0c7-0a010f14b7ca" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186077469 #edb/ref 1080 "11.0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186077469 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186077469 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a1b81862-5146-5f0a-8ac5-0fd79c0a2c35" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186077470 #edb/ref 1080 "9.8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186077470 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186077470 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "cf368945-778b-5d74-90d6-d2b82979f4cc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186077471 #edb/ref 1080 "12.8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186077471 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186077471 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "fe7a84db-08fb-51e4-b38d-a6f78cb89655" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186077472 #edb/ref 1080 "11.8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186077472 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186077472 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0ed5b9e8-a40d-55c4-8a76-c92577e695bc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186077473 #edb/ref 1080 "10.5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186077473 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186077473 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "36c4bd36-3076-50a5-a9a1-65ac22047faa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078256 #edb/ref 1069 "e-3248" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078256 #edb/ref 1071 "Given the triangle below, find the length of $\\overline{MN}$ rounded to one decimal place. \n\n![](images/db/db0c3be4d3f18a55bfbd763e4017bdabd6c27ba7b498e21909baa4aea3d44337.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078256 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "17e8ec56-6fda-5294-b27c-9b3e312a5f75" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078256 #edb/ref 1074 "For an angle $\\theta$ in a right triangle, the trigonometric ratios are as follows:\n\n- $\\sin\\theta = \\dfrac{\\textrm{opposite leg}}{\\textrm{hypotenuse}}$\n\n- $\\cos\\theta = \\dfrac{\\textrm{adjacent leg}}{\\textrm{hypotenuse}}$\n\n- $\\tan\\theta = \\dfrac{\\textrm{opposite leg}}{\\textrm{adjacent leg}}$\n\nFirst, note that we are given the length of the hypotenuse $\\overline{NO}$ and wish to find the length of the leg $\\overline{MN}$ adjacent to the given angle $\\angle{N}.$\n\nThe trigonometric ratio that relates the adjacent leg to the hypotenuse is *cosine*. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(m∠N) & =\\frac{\\text{adjacent leg}}{\\text{hypotenuse}} \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡({25}^{∘}) & =\\frac{MN}{14} \\\\ MN & =14\\operatorname{cos}⁡({25}^{∘}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing a calculator to evaluate the trigonometric ratio, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}MN & =14\\operatorname{cos}⁡({25}^{∘}) \\\\  & =14(0.906\\,30…) \\\\  & =12.688\\,30… \\\\  & ≈12.7,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to one decimal place." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078257 #edb/ref 1069 "e-3249" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078257 #edb/ref 1071 "Given the triangle below, find the length of $\\overline{NO}$ rounded to one decimal place.\n\n![](images/91/9108818debc297388dde73a7aa7689eac263c6ec033643c7e2bcdfb3677a8f44.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078257 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b4f8dd38-d62d-5940-b936-48f68e0693b8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078257 #edb/ref 1074 "For an angle $\\theta$ in a right triangle, the trigonometric ratios are as follows:\n\n- $\\sin\\theta = \\dfrac{\\textrm{opposite leg}}{\\textrm{hypotenuse}}$\n\n- $\\cos\\theta = \\dfrac{\\textrm{adjacent leg}}{\\textrm{hypotenuse}}$\n\n- $\\tan\\theta = \\dfrac{\\textrm{opposite leg}}{\\textrm{adjacent leg}}$\n\nFirst, notice that we are given the length of the leg $\\overline{MO}$ opposite the given angle $\\angle{N}$ and wish to find the length of the hypotenuse $\\overline{NO}.$\n\nThe trigonometric ratio that relates the opposite leg to the hypotenuse is *sine*. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(m∠N) & =\\frac{\\text{opposite leg}}{\\text{hypotenuse}} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡({32}^{∘}) & =\\frac{20}{NO} \\\\ NO\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡({32}^{∘}) & =20 \\\\ NO & =\\frac{20}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡({32}^{∘})}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing a calculator to evaluate the trigonometric ratio, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}NO & =\\frac{20}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡({32}^{∘})} \\\\  & =\\frac{20}{(0.529\\,91…)} \\\\  & =37.741\\,59… \\\\  & ≈37.7,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to one decimal place." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078258 #edb/ref 1069 "e-3250" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078258 #edb/ref 1071 "Given the triangle below, find the length of $\\overline{BC}$ in terms of $\\theta.$\n\n![](images/8b/8b1f3d7e1d87c7021970f45279bb404b4e9998a9d351d1e95616dac98f80d45d.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078258 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a74a938e-94a4-5a91-aced-4955dc8dfbf8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078258 #edb/ref 1074 "For an angle $\\theta$ in a right triangle, the trigonometric ratios are as follows:\n\n- $\\sin\\theta = \\dfrac{\\textrm{opposite leg}}{\\textrm{hypotenuse}}$\n\n- $\\cos\\theta = \\dfrac{\\textrm{adjacent leg}}{\\textrm{hypotenuse}}$\n\n- $\\tan\\theta = \\dfrac{\\textrm{opposite leg}}{\\textrm{adjacent leg}}$\n\nNotice that we are given the length of the leg $\\overline{AB}$ adjacent to the given angle $\\angle A$ and wish to find the length of the leg $\\overline{BC}$ opposite $\\angle A.$\n\nThe trigonometric ratio that relates the opposite leg to the adjacent leg is *tangent*. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A) & =\\frac{\\text{opposite leg}}{\\text{adjacent leg}} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{BC}{15} \\\\ BC & =15\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078551 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048438 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078551 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049915 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078551 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186078816 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078551 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186078829 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078551 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186079115 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078551 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186519519 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078551 #edb/ref 1039 "Calculating an Unknown Side Length Using Sine" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078551 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186078257 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078551 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "04354ab1-c6ec-534e-bb57-267f326c15fc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078552 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186078727 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078552 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186078830 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078552 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186079116 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078552 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186519547 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078552 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186519553 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078552 #edb/ref 1039 "Calculating an Unknown Side Length Using Cosine" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078552 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186078256 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078552 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "9afe0d46-84e7-5937-9b42-170097a72493" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078553 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186078725 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078553 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186078954 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078553 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186079112 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078553 #edb/ref 1038 #ed